invariant: INV-16
file: keysched.h
catches: hash_runtime_exporter_test
reason: ks_exporter_cpu calls the copy on the instructions for a value that
  does not name them, and keysched.c for one that does, so ch_export in a
  session without CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256 runs SHA-256 instructions
  over the exporter secret (docs/decisions.md 93). The bytes are the same.
  A QUIC object holds no exporter, so bin/hash_runtime_exporter_test, the
  counting test built as a TCP object with the exporter, is the binary
  that holds this entry's row.

--- old
    if (hash_on_instructions(cpu, hash_len)) {
        ks_exporter_hw(hash_len, exp_master, label, context, context_len, out, out_len);
--- new
    if (!hash_on_instructions(cpu, hash_len)) {
        ks_exporter_hw(hash_len, exp_master, label, context, context_len, out, out_len);
